			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Enable .app bundle resource resolution for cache, Cocoon, and Node\n\nThe Mountain binary now resolves pre-baked resources from both the repo/dev\nlayout (binary-sibling files) and the .app bundle layout (Contents/Resources/)\nwhen running as a packaged application. Four systems are updated:\n\n**Extension manifest cache (LoadFromCache.rs):** Probes two locations in\norder — `BinaryDir/extensions.manifest.json` (dev) and\n`BinaryDir/../Resources/extensions.manifest.json` (bundle). Bundled caches\nskip the staleness check (10-minute threshold) since they are built\nalongside the .app and always consistent with its packed extensions. The\nper-manifest field extraction is also refactored with local `str()` and\n`arr()` helper closures to eliminate repeated\n`Manifest.get(k).and_then(Value::as_str)` chains.\n\n**CocoonManagement pre-flight check:** Cocoon's bundle probe now attempts\nTauri's resource resolver first (`Tauri::path::resolve` with\n`BaseDirectory::Resource`), falling back to the repo-layout relative-walk\nfrom `scripts/cocoon/` when the bundle path does not exist.\n\n**NodeResolver TryShipped:** Adds a sidecar resolution path matching\n`externalBin: [\"Binary/node\"]` in tauri.conf.json — the `node` binary sits\nalongside the Mountain executable, not in a `Node/bin/` subdirectory, in\nthe Tauri sidecar layout.\n\n**ScanPathConfigure and PathSecurity:** Extension scan paths now call\n`.canonicalize()` on resolved paths for cleaner log output (showing\n`Contents/Resources/...` instead of `Contents/MacOS/../Resources/...`).\n`IsTrustedSystemPath` adds `../Resources/Static/Application/extensions` to\nthe bundle-root allowlist so the new canonical static extension directory\nbypasses the workspace-folder gate.\n\n**Bootstrap fork (bootstrap-fork.js):** Cocoon entry path resolution\nhandles both bundle (2-level `../../`) and repo (3-level `../../../`)\nlayouts by iterating both URL bases for each candidate entry path.\n\n**tauri.conf.json:** Maps `bootstrap-fork.js`, `extensions.manifest.json`,\nand `Cocoon/Target/Bootstrap/Implementation/Cocoon` into\n`Contents/Resources/` so all three are reachable at runtime via the bundle\nresource resolver.",
